        "created_at": "2011-09-25T14:08:42.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Sub-Zero Atmosphere causes villain cards which would act at the end of the villain turn to instead act at the start of the villain turn.</p>\n<p>Omnitron flips at the start of his turn and does something different on the end of his turn depending on which side he’s on.</p>\n<p>We decided that with Sub-Zero Atmosphere in play, then at the start of Omnitron’s turn we had a choice as to the order of him flipping vs getting a villain card, so we chose to have him flip first. Then, having flipped, the normal end of turn action of getting a villain card from his other side became a start of turn action and got triggered. I figure that if we’d done things in the other order, we would have needlessly been causing Omnitron’s normal end of turn action from BOTH SIDES of his card every turn.</p>\n<p>Have I interpreted this correctly?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:34:48.396Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 1,
